Add ic_history_save() to persist programmatic history changes.

The history file is written when ic_readline() returns, and nothing else in
the public API can write it. ic_history_add(), ic_history_remove_last() and
ic_history_clear() therefore only mutate the in-memory list: the change is
visible to the current session but is undone by the next automatic save, or
lost entirely if the program exits first.

clox hits this when dropping REPL commands from the history -- the entry is
already on disk by the time ic_readline() hands the line back, so removing it
in memory is not enough.

This exposes the existing history_save() as ic_history_save(). Purely
additive: no existing behaviour changes, and the automatic save on the
ic_readline() path is untouched.

Upstream: https://github.com/daanx/isocline at tag v1.1.0
Apply with: git apply -p1  # from clox/vendor/isocline/, after 0001

--- a/include/isocline.h
+++ b/include/isocline.h
@@ -140,6 +140,13 @@
 /// Add an entry to the history
 void ic_history_add( const char* entry );
 
+/// Save the history to the file set with `ic_set_history()`.
+/// The history is saved automatically when `ic_readline()` returns, so this is
+/// only needed to persist changes made programmatically with `ic_history_add()`,
+/// `ic_history_remove_last()`, or `ic_history_clear()`.
+/// Does nothing if no history file was set.
+void ic_history_save(void);
+
 /// \}
 
 //--------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/src/isocline.c
+++ b/src/isocline.c
@@ -228,6 +228,11 @@
   history_clear(env->history);
 }
 
+ic_public void ic_history_save(void) {
+  ic_env_t* env = ic_get_env(); if (env==NULL) return;
+  history_save(env->history);
+}
